  "title": "Congress’s Social Media 💩 Show Congress’s social media hearing was a ...",
  "description": "Congress’s Social Media 💩 Show Congress’s social media hearing was a sh*tshow at best that included throwing racist accusations of being a Chinese operative at the Singaporian CEO of TikTok, forcing a bland and robotic apology out of Mark Zuckerberg for his platforms’ fatally harmful effects on teens, and throwing the blame squarely at the feet of social media companies saying they had blood on their hands, despite no legislative action being taken to address any of the problems. Instead the so-called lawmakers were more focused on creating clippable viral moments of their hollow grandstanding so they could trend on the very same platforms they’re accusing of being harmful to children. And nobody is doubting those accusations are true, there are mountains of evidence to support that. But when your only real proposed answer is trying to resurrect the Kids online safety act, a bill that would significantly increase surveillance, restrict access to information, and trample on free speech, rather than addressing things like healthcare, food insecurity, or climate change to name a few: Its pretty clear they couldn’t give less of a f*ck about actually protecting kids online or off. #congress #socialmedia #congressionalhearing #kosa #onlinesafety #politics #satire #news #comedy #comedynews #funews #usnews ",
